<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Mu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 229 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Mu was a general of the State of Zhao in the 3rd century BCE. Stationed on the northern frontier, he destroyed a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> army in the 240s BCE, and he later defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> invasions in 233 and 232 BCE. In 229 BCE a Qin bribe led the Zhao court to remove and execute him, and Zhao fell to Qin the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/li-mu.jpg" alt="Li Mu" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Li_Mu1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
